From c530fae2097a22c7320f59562623f78d456e9584 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Simon Polack <spolack+git@mailbox.org>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 21:49:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] W5500 receive path for wire-speed bursts, application hook,
 diagnostics

Receive (src/device.rs):
- Bulk reads: what waits in the chip is read in chunks of up to CHUNK
  (4 KB) per SPI transaction into a receive buffer of BULK bytes, and the
  chip gets the space back at once. Frames are then served from that
  buffer. The original used 8 SPI transactions per frame, too slow for
  wire-speed bursts.
- Background reads: the next chunk transfers (DMA) while the frames of the
  current one are handled, through the new BulkRead trait (src/lib.rs):
  bulk_start, bulk_finish, bulk_error.
- Partial frames at the end of a chunk are kept and completed by the next.
- Received size: the interrupt is cleared before RX_RSR is read (the other
  order lost the wake-up of a frame landing in between), and RX_RSR is read
  until two values match, at most 4 rounds (the chip writes a frame's
  length header last).
- Resync: a frame length that makes no sense drops the batch and re-reads
  the chip's pointer (RX_RESYNCS).
- Application hook: BulkRead::rx_hook sees every frame straight from the
  receive buffer; returning true takes it and it never reaches the network
  stack. The driver yields every 8 taken frames.
- The receive buffer comes from BulkRead::take_rx_buffer, so the
  application places it.

Transmit: write_frame is bounded and yields: a TX buffer that never drains
(link down, a glitch) drops the frame after 20 ms instead of hanging.

Runner (src/lib.rs):
- Queued TX frames are sent before more frames are read.
- Does not wait for the interrupt line while frames of the current batch
  are still unread (rx_pending).
- read_frame returning 0 (nothing complete) is not handed up; an SPI error
  counts in SPI_CHECK_ERRORS and backs off 1 ms instead of spinning.

Link check and counters:
- is_link_up also reads the version register as a running SPI check
  (SPI_CHECKS, SPI_CHECK_ERRORS) and notices a chip that lost its socket
  setup (CHIP_RESET_SEEN), e.g. after a power glitch.
- RX_BACKLOG_MAX: largest backlog seen at the start of a batch.

Only the W5500 is used and tested.
